// The common early-return guard: after `if d == 0 { return }`, the negated fact
// `d != 0` carries to the rest of the function, so the later divide proves safe.
// DECIDE-M (2026-09-28): a signed quotient needs one bit more than its operands — `a / b`
// with a possibly TYPE_MIN dividend over a divisor that may be -1 is 2^31, which no i32
// holds (and was a C division trapping at -O0, a silent value at -O2). The result is i64
// here so this test stays about what it tests: the divisor.
func f(x i32, d i32) i64 {
    if d == 0 {
        return -1
    }
    return x / d
}
func main() i32 { return 0 }
